# Real-World Incident
A SaaS billing portal exposed invoices when an endpoint accepted an arbitrary customerId parameter; attackers enumerated IDs to download other customers’ invoices.

## Vulnerable Implementation

```java
package com.example.documents;

import org.springframework.core.io.FileSystemResource;
import org.springframework.core.io.Resource;
import org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;

// VULNERABLE: IDOR (Insecure Direct Object Reference)
// CVE: CVE-2024-22234 (Spring Authorization bypass patterns)
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/documents")
public class VulnerableDocumentController {

    private static final String DOCUMENT_DIR = "/var/data/documents";

    @GetMapping("/download")
    public ResponseEntity<Resource> downloadDocument(
            @RequestParam Long documentId,
            @RequestParam Long userId) {  // VULNERABLE: Trusts client-supplied userId

        // VULNERABLE: No authorization check - assumes client sends correct userId
        // Attacker can change userId parameter to access other users' documents
        Path documentPath = Paths.get(DOCUMENT_DIR,
            "doc_" + documentId + "_user_" + userId + ".pdf");

        Resource resource = new FileSystemResource(documentPath);

        if (!resource.exists()) {
            return ResponseEntity.notFound().build();
        }

        // Returns document without verifying ownership
        return ResponseEntity.ok()
            .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION,
                "attachment; filename="document.pdf"")
            .body(resource);
    }

    @GetMapping("/{documentId}/metadata")
    public DocumentMetadata getMetadata(
            @PathVariable Long documentId,
            @RequestParam Long requestingUserId) {  // VULNERABLE: Trusts client

        // VULNERABLE: No check that documentId belongs to requestingUserId
        return documentRepository.findById(documentId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("Document not found"));
    }
}
```

**Attack Demonstration:**
```bash
# Attack 1: Access another user's document by changing userId parameter
curl "http://api.example.com/api/documents/download?documentId=1234&userId=999"
# Attacker provides their own userId, system doesn't verify it matches authenticated user

# Attack 2: Enumerate all documents by iterating document IDs
for i in {1..10000}; do
  curl -O "http://api.example.com/api/documents/download?documentId=$i&userId=999"
done
# Downloads thousands of documents belonging to other users

# Attack 3: Access document metadata without authorization
curl "http://api.example.com/api/documents/1234/metadata?requestingUserId=999"
# Returns sensitive metadata for documents the attacker doesn't own
```

## Common Mistakes

1. **Client-side authorization checks only** — Hiding UI elements but not enforcing access control on the server. Attackers bypass the frontend entirely with direct API calls.

2. **Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR)** — Using sequential IDs (user/1, user/2) without verifying the requesting user owns the resource. Always validate resource ownership server-side.

3. **Missing function-level access control** — Checking authentication but not authorization. A logged-in regular user should not access admin endpoints just because they are authenticated.

4. **Trusting JWT claims without verification** — Reading role or permissions from JWT payload without verifying the signature, or accepting tokens from untrusted issuers.

## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Fix (5 minutes)

Use server-side authorization checks. Never trust client-provided user IDs.

```java
// SECURE Tier 1: Server-side authorization check (5 minutes)
package com.example.documents;

import org.springframework.core.io.Resource;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/secure/documents")
public class SecureTier1DocumentController {

    private final DocumentService documentService;

    public SecureTier1DocumentController(DocumentService documentService) {
        this.documentService = documentService;
    }

    @GetMapping("/download")
    public ResponseEntity<Resource> downloadDocument(
            @RequestParam Long documentId,
            Authentication auth) {  // Use Spring Security Authentication

        // SECURE: Get userId from authenticated session (not request parameter)
        Long authenticatedUserId = ((UserPrincipal) auth.getPrincipal()).getId();

        // Verify document belongs to authenticated user
        Document document = documentService.getDocument(documentId);
        if (!document.getOwnerId().equals(authenticatedUserId)) {
            throw new ForbiddenException("Access denied");
        }

        Resource resource = documentService.loadDocumentAsResource(documentId);
        return ResponseEntity.ok()
            .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION,
                "attachment; filename="" + document.getFilename() + """)
            .body(resource);
    }
}
```

**Why This Works:** User identity comes from authenticated session (not request parameters). Server verifies document ownership before allowing access.

### Tier 2: Essential Defenses (15 minutes)

Add repository-level authorization and comprehensive audit logging.

```java
// SECURE Tier 2: Repository-level authorization + audit logging (15 minutes)
package com.example.documents;

import org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/secure/documents")
public class SecureTier2DocumentController {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SecureTier2DocumentController.class);
    private final DocumentService documentService;
    private final AuditService auditService;

    public SecureTier2DocumentController(DocumentService documentService, AuditService auditService) {
        this.documentService = documentService;
        this.auditService = auditService;
    }

    @GetMapping("/download")
    public ResponseEntity<Resource> downloadDocument(
            @RequestParam Long documentId,
            Authentication auth,
            HttpServletRequest request) {

        Long userId = ((UserPrincipal) auth.getPrincipal()).getId();
        String userEmail = auth.getName();

        // Repository method enforces authorization at data layer
        Document document = documentService.getDocumentForUser(documentId, userId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> {
                // Log unauthorized access attempt
                log.warn("Unauthorized document access attempt: user={}, documentId={}, ip={}",
                        userEmail, documentId, request.getRemoteAddr());
                auditService.logUnauthorizedAccess(userId, documentId, request.getRemoteAddr());
                return new ForbiddenException("Access denied");
            });

        // Audit successful access
        auditService.logDocumentAccess(userId, documentId, "download", request.getRemoteAddr());
        log.info("Document downloaded: user={}, documentId={}", userEmail, documentId);

        Resource resource = documentService.loadDocumentAsResource(documentId);
        return ResponseEntity.ok()
            .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION,
                "attachment; filename="" + document.getFilename() + """)
            .body(resource);
    }
}

@Repository
public interface DocumentRepository extends JpaRepository<Document, Long> {
    // Authorization enforced at query level
    @Query("SELECT d FROM Document d WHERE d.id = :docId AND d.ownerId = :userId")
    Optional<Document> findByIdAndOwner(@Param("docId") Long documentId, @Param("userId") Long userId);
}
```

**Additional Defenses:**
- Authorization enforced at database query level
- Audit logging for all access attempts (authorized and unauthorized)
- Failed access attempts logged with IP addresses
- Spring Security Authentication used for user identity

### Tier 3: Production Hardening (30 minutes)

Implement comprehensive IDOR protection including enumeration detection.

```java
// SECURE Tier 3: Comprehensive IDOR protection (30 minutes)
package com.example.documents;

import io.micrometer.core.instrument.Counter;
import io.micrometer.core.instrument.MeterRegistry;
import org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/secure/documents")
public class SecureTier3DocumentController {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SecureTier3DocumentController.class);
    private final DocumentService documentService;
    private final AuditService auditService;
    private final Counter idorAttempts;
    private final Counter unauthorizedAccess;
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, RateLimitEntry> rateLimiter = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public SecureTier3DocumentController(DocumentService documentService,
                                          AuditService auditService,
                                          MeterRegistry registry) {
        this.documentService = documentService;
        this.auditService = auditService;
        this.idorAttempts = Counter.builder("security.idor.attempts")
            .description("IDOR attack attempts detected")
            .tag("endpoint", "/api/documents/download")
            .register(registry);
        this.unauthorizedAccess = Counter.builder("security.unauthorized_access")
            .description("Unauthorized resource access attempts")
            .register(registry);
    }

    @GetMapping("/download")
    public ResponseEntity<Resource> downloadDocument(
            @RequestParam Long documentId,
            Authentication auth,
            HttpServletRequest request) {

        Long userId = ((UserPrincipal) auth.getPrincipal()).getId();
        String userEmail = auth.getName();
        String clientIp = request.getRemoteAddr();

        // Rate limiting: Prevent enumeration attacks
        String rateLimitKey = userId + ":" + clientIp;
        if (isRateLimited(rateLimitKey)) {
            log.warn("Rate limit exceeded: user={}, ip={}", userEmail, clientIp);
            throw new TooManyRequestsException("Rate limit exceeded");
        }

        // Validate document ID is positive
        if (documentId == null || documentId <= 0) {
            log.warn("Invalid document ID: {}", documentId);
            throw new BadRequestException("Invalid document ID");
        }

        // Check authorization at repository level
        Document document = documentService.getDocumentForUser(documentId, userId)
            .orElseGet(() -> {
                // Log and alert on unauthorized access
                idorAttempts.increment();
                unauthorizedAccess.increment();
                log.error("IDOR attempt detected: user={} attempted access to document={} from ip={}",
                         userEmail, documentId, clientIp);
                auditService.logIdorAttempt(userId, documentId, clientIp);

                // Check if this user is systematically enumerating documents
                if (auditService.getRecentIdorAttempts(userId) > 10) {
                    log.error("Multiple IDOR attempts from user={}, triggering security review", userEmail);
                    auditService.triggerSecurityAlert(userId, "IDOR_ENUMERATION");
                }

                throw new ForbiddenException("Access denied");
            });

        // Verify document is not in deleted/archived state
        if (document.getStatus() != DocumentStatus.ACTIVE) {
            throw new ForbiddenException("Document not accessible");
        }

        // Check if document has additional access restrictions
        if (document.getAccessLevel() == AccessLevel.RESTRICTED) {
            if (!documentService.hasRestrictedAccess(userId, documentId)) {
                log.warn("Restricted document access denied: user={}, doc={}", userEmail, documentId);
                throw new ForbiddenException("Insufficient permissions");
            }
        }

        // Audit successful access
        auditService.logDocumentAccess(userId, documentId, "download", clientIp);
        log.info("Document downloaded: user={}, doc={}, filename={}",
                userEmail, documentId, document.getFilename());

        Resource resource = documentService.loadDocumentAsResource(documentId);
        return ResponseEntity.ok()
            .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION,
                "attachment; filename="" + document.getFilename() + """)
            .header("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")
            .body(resource);
    }

    private boolean isRateLimited(String key) {
        RateLimitEntry entry = rateLimiter.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new RateLimitEntry());
        Instant now = Instant.now();

        // Allow 20 downloads per minute
        if (now.isAfter(entry.windowStart.plusSeconds(60))) {
            entry.count = 1;
            entry.windowStart = now;
            return false;
        }

        entry.count++;
        return entry.count > 20;
    }

    private static class RateLimitEntry {
        int count = 0;
        Instant windowStart = Instant.now();
    }
}
```

**Production Controls:**
- Rate limiting to prevent document enumeration
- Enumeration detection (multiple failed access attempts)
- Prometheus metrics for IDOR attack attempts
- Comprehensive audit trail with IP logging
- Security alerts on repeated IDOR attempts
- Document status and access level validation

## Testing

```java
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
public class DocumentControllerSecurityTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "user1", userId = "1")
    public void testVulnerableCodeExploitable_AccessOtherUserDocument() throws Exception {
        // Verify IDOR vulnerability allows access to other user's documents
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/documents/download")
                .param("documentId", "100")
                .param("userId", "999"))  // Attacker changes userId
            .andExpect(status().isOk());  // Vulnerable: Returns document
    }

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "user1", userId = "1")
    public void testTier1BlocksIDOR() throws Exception {
        // Verify server-side check prevents IDOR
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/secure/documents/download")
                .param("documentId", "100"))
            .andExpect(status().isForbidden())
            .andExpect(content().string(containsString("Access denied")));
    }

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "user1", userId = "1")
    public void testTier2AuditLogging() throws Exception {
        // Verify unauthorized access is logged
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/secure/documents/download")
                .param("documentId", "999"));

        // Check audit log was created
        verify(auditService).logUnauthorizedAccess(eq(1L), eq(999L), anyString());
    }

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "attacker", userId = "666")
    public void testTier3EnumerationDetection() throws Exception {
        // Simulate enumeration attack (trying many document IDs)
        for (int i = 1; i <= 15; i++) {
            mockMvc.perform(get("/api/secure/documents/download")
                    .param("documentId", String.valueOf(i)))
                .andExpect(status().isForbidden());
        }

        // Verify security alert triggered
        verify(auditService).triggerSecurityAlert(eq(666L), eq("IDOR_ENUMERATION"));
    }

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "user1", userId = "1")
    public void testTier3RateLimiting() throws Exception {
        // Verify rate limiting prevents rapid enumeration
        for (int i = 0; i < 25; i++) {
            ResultActions result = mockMvc.perform(get("/api/secure/documents/download")
                    .param("documentId", "100"));

            if (i < 20) {
                result.andExpect(status().isAnyOf(200, 403));  // Allowed
            } else {
                result.andExpect(status().is(429));  // Rate limited
            }
        }
    }

    @Test
    @WithMockUser(username = "owner", userId = "1")
    public void testLegitimateAccessWorks() throws Exception {
        // Verify legitimate owner can download their document
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/secure/documents/download")
                .param("documentId", "1"))  // User 1's document
            .andExpect(status().isOk())
            .andExpect(header().exists("Content-Disposition"));
    }
}
```

## Monitoring & Alerting

```yaml
# Prometheus Alerting Rules for IDOR

groups:
  - name: idor_alerts
    interval: 30s
    rules:
      - alert: IDORAttackDetected
        expr: rate(security_idor_attempts_total[5m]) > 0.5
        for: 2m
        labels:
          severity: critical
          category: authorization
        annotations:
          summary: "IDOR attack attempts detected"
          description: "{{ $value }} IDOR attempts per second over last 5 minutes"

      - alert: UnauthorizedAccessSpike
        expr: rate(security_unauthorized_access_total[5m]) > 5
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: high
          category: authorization
        annotations:
          summary: "High rate of unauthorized access attempts"
          description: "{{ $value }} unauthorized access attempts per second"

      - alert: DocumentEnumerationDetected
        expr: sum(rate(security_idor_attempts_total[1m])) by (user_id) > 10
        for: 2m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Document enumeration attack from user {{ $labels.user_id }}"
          description: "User attempting systematic document ID enumeration"

      - alert: SuspiciousDocumentAccessPattern
        expr: rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{uri="/api/documents/download",status="403"}[5m]) > 10
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High rate of forbidden document access attempts"
          description: "{{ $value }} forbidden responses per second may indicate scanning"

# Grafana Dashboard Queries
# 1. IDOR Attempts: sum(rate(security_idor_attempts_total[5m]))
# 2. Unauthorized Access: sum(rate(security_unauthorized_access_total[5m]))
# 3. Access Success Rate: rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{status="200"}[5m]) / rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count[5m])
# 4. Top Attackers: topk(10, sum by (client_ip) (rate(security_idor_attempts_total[1h])))
```

## Incident Response

```markdown
# Incident Response: IDOR Attack Detected

## Detection

**Indicators:**
- Prometheus alert: `IDORAttackDetected` or `DocumentEnumerationDetected` fired
- Application logs show: `IDOR attempt detected: user=X attempted access to document=Y`
- High rate of 403 Forbidden responses for document downloads
- Audit logs show user accessing documents they don't own

**Static Analysis:**
```bash
# Check for authorization bypass vulnerabilities
semgrep --config=p/owasp-top-ten --include="*Controller.java" src/
grep -r "@RequestParam.*userId" src/  # Find client-controlled auth parameters
```

**Runtime Detection:**
```bash
# Check for IDOR attempts in logs
grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | tail -100
grep "Access denied" /var/log/app.log | wc -l  # Count unauthorized attempts
```

## Containment (Immediate - <15 minutes)

**1. Identify Attacking Users:**
```bash
# Extract attacker user IDs from logs
grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | awk '{print $6}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr

# Get attacker IPs
grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | grep -oE "ip=[0-9.]+" | sort | uniq -c
```

**2. Suspend Attacking Accounts:**
```sql
-- Temporarily disable accounts
UPDATE users SET account_status = 'SUSPENDED', suspension_reason = 'IDOR_ATTACK_DETECTED'
WHERE user_id IN (666, 777, 888);

-- Invalidate active sessions
DELETE FROM user_sessions WHERE user_id IN (666, 777, 888);
```

**3. Block Attacking IPs:**
```bash
# Firewall block
for ip in 10.1.1.100 10.1.1.101; do
  iptables -A INPUT -s $ip -j DROP
done

# WAF block
aws wafv2 update-ip-set --id IP_SET_ID --addresses 10.1.1.100/32 10.1.1.101/32
```

**4. Enable Enhanced Logging:**
```yaml
# Temporarily enable debug logging for authorization
logging:
  level:
    com.example.documents: DEBUG
    org.springframework.security: DEBUG
```

## Investigation (1-4 hours)

**1. Identify Compromised Documents:**
```sql
-- Find documents accessed by attackers
SELECT document_id, owner_id, accessed_by_user_id, access_timestamp, client_ip
FROM audit_log
WHERE accessed_by_user_id IN (666, 777, 888)
  AND accessed_by_user_id != owner_id  -- Unauthorized access
  AND timestamp > 'ATTACK_START_TIME'
ORDER BY timestamp;
```

**2. Count Exposed Documents:**
```sql
-- How many documents were exposed?
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT document_id) as exposed_count,
       COUNT(*) as total_accesses
FROM audit_log
WHERE accessed_by_user_id IN (ATTACKER_IDS)
  AND accessed_by_user_id != owner_id
  AND timestamp > 'ATTACK_START_TIME';
```

**3. Identify Affected Document Owners:**
```sql
-- Which users' documents were accessed?
SELECT DISTINCT d.owner_id, u.email, COUNT(DISTINCT d.document_id) as docs_accessed
FROM audit_log a
JOIN documents d ON a.document_id = d.document_id
JOIN users u ON d.owner_id = u.user_id
WHERE a.accessed_by_user_id IN (ATTACKER_IDS)
  AND a.accessed_by_user_id != d.owner_id
GROUP BY d.owner_id, u.email
ORDER BY docs_accessed DESC;
```

**4. Check for Data Exfiltration:**
```bash
# Large document downloads
grep "Document downloaded" /var/log/app.log | grep "user=attacker" | awk '{print $NF}' | sort | uniq

# Download volume by attacker
grep "user=attacker.*Document downloaded" /var/log/app.log | wc -l
```

**5. Timeline Reconstruction:**
```bash
# When did the attack start/end?
grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | head -1  # First attempt
grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | tail -1  # Last attempt

# Attack duration
start=$(grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | head -1 | awk '{print $1}')
end=$(grep "IDOR attempt" /var/log/app.log | tail -1 | awk '{print $1}')
echo "Attack duration: $start to $end"
```

## Remediation (4-24 hours)

**1. Deploy Secure Implementation:**
```bash
# Deploy Tier 3 secure code
git checkout -b hotfix/idor-fix
# Apply secure implementation with authorization checks
git commit -m "fix: Prevent IDOR with server-side authorization + rate limiting"
git push origin hotfix/idor-fix

# Emergency deployment
kubectl set image deployment/document-service document-service=myregistry/document-service:v2.1.0-secure
kubectl rollout status deployment/document-service
```

**2. Verify Authorization on All Endpoints:**
```bash
# Audit all endpoints for authorization checks
grep -r "@GetMapping" src/ | grep -v "Authentication"  # Find endpoints without auth
```

**3. Deploy Enhanced Monitoring:**
```yaml
# Apply Prometheus rules
kubectl apply -f prometheus-rules/idor-alerts.yaml

# Enable audit logging
kubectl patch configmap app-config --patch '{"data":{"audit.level":"DEBUG"}}'
```

**4. Implement Rate Limiting:**
```yaml
# Rate limit document downloads
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: rate-limits
data:
  document-downloads: "20 per minute per user"
```

## Post-Incident (24-72 hours)

**1. Notify Affected Users:**
```sql
# Generate notification list
SELECT DISTINCT u.email, u.user_id
FROM users u
WHERE u.user_id IN (
  SELECT DISTINCT d.owner_id
  FROM audit_log a
  JOIN documents d ON a.document_id = d.document_id
  WHERE a.accessed_by_user_id IN (ATTACKER_IDS)
    AND a.accessed_by_user_id != d.owner_id
);
```

Email template:
```
